+#  and produced NOTHING, so "no features found" was indistinguishable from a
+#  crash. One genome in 1356 (11292.18743) hit this.
+#  Per JJD: a genome that matched a rep contig but called no features is still
+#  worth recording. The BLASTn hit says which taxon was selected and how
+#  strongly, and that belongs in the GTO even with an empty feature set.
+#
+#  It has to be emitted here, because annotate_by_viral_pssm-GTO.pl reads the
+#  close-genome fields (columns 12-16) off the FEATURE ROWS of this script's
+#  stdout. No rows meant $close_id, $close_name, $close_bit and $viral_family
+#  all stayed undef, and the GTO came back with an empty close_genomes entry
+#  and no viral_family -- the taxon assignment silently lost.
+#
+#  The row carries feature type "no_features_called", which the GTO parser
+#  picks up for close_genomes and viral_family but does NOT turn into a
